    <!-- ── Heatmap / Brain Screen ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <string name="brain_title">THE BRAIN</string>
    <string name="brain_subtitle">30 Juz  \u00b7  Memory Decay Dashboard</string>
    <string name="help_brain_title">How The Brain Works</string>
    <string name="help_brain_desc">The Brain is your intelligent memorization assistant. It uses a scientific model (FSRS) to predict how well you remember every page.\n\n\u25cf <b>Stability (Colors)</b>: Green means the page is solid in your memory. Yellow/Red means it is fading and needs revision soon.\n\n\u25cf <b>Symmetry</b>: The app rewards you more if you revise a page right before you forget it. Revising too early provides a smaller boost to long-term memory.\n\n\u25cf <b>Forecast Slider</b>: Move the slider at the top to travel through time! See which pages will turn red in 7, 14, or 30 days if you don\'t revise them.\n\n\u25cf <b>Semantic Interference</b>: If you struggle with a verse in the Vault (Mutashabihat), the app automatically lowers the stability of similar verses elsewhere, as they are likely confusion points.\n\n\u25cf <b>Revision Debt</b>: The number of pages that have fallen below 50% stability.\n\n\u25cf <b>Recovery Goal</b>: The number of pages you need to revise daily to turn your entire Brain green within a month.</string>
